  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">223420_Pre-Action project_Start Ready Risk Pool 3 : Zimbabwe Drought 2024 season (Masvingo)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To improve the communities preparedness to shocks, the project will: 
 
 1. Establish and strengthen Early Warning, Weather and Climate information dissemination systems. 
 
 2. Develop and implement a robust community preparedness and capacity strengthening curriculum.
 
 3. 3.Water management (water conservation and alternative water sources including mechanization) 
 
 Agricultural Practices: i) Drought-Resistant Crops: Encourage the cultivation of drought-resistant crop varieties that require less water and are more resilient to dry conditions e.g. pearl millet, finger millet, sorghum, groundnuts, Bambara nuts, sunflower, and sesame. ii) Soil Management: Implement soil conservation practices such as mulching, contour plowing, and agroforestry to retain soil moisture and improve soil health. iii) Diversified Livelihoods: Promote diversified livelihoods, including the introduction of alternative income-generating activities such as poultry farming, beekeeping, or crafts, to reduce dependence on rain-fed agriculture. iv) Promote water efficient irrigation systems that include installation of drip irrigation systems at community gardens where women and youths will have access to irrigable land and produce crops under irrigation. v) Establishment of vertical farms and potted plants that are water efficient and allow production of vegetables for household consumption with low investment costs. vi) Encourage the production of diverse nutrition rich horticultural crops in nutritional gardens. 
 
 5. Livestock Management(Establish fodder banks to store feed for livestock during dry periods and to implement veterinary health programs to keep livestock healthy and resilient to the stress of drought and provision of drinking water through troughs.</narrative>
  </description>
